@startuml activity-ml_lifecycle
title training the classifier and returning decisions to it
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor Black
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor Black
  FontColor Black
  DiamondBackgroundColor White
  DiamondBorderColor Black
  DiamondFontColor Black
  StartColor Black
  EndColor Black
  BarColor Black
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor Black
  FontColor Black
}
skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor Black
  TitleFontColor Black
}

|me|
start
:download the pose archive;
:extract into the gitignored data path;
:select the 47 labelled files;
note right
  keypoints arrive already extracted, 17 points per
  person with tracker ids and boxes attached, so no
  video-to-pose step runs in this project
end note

|notebook|
repeat
  :cut 30-frame windows at stride 15;
  :normalize keypoints against each bounding box;
  note right
    normalization is box relative, so absolute screen
    position cannot become a feature and the model does
    not bind itself to one camera angle
  end note
  :train the two-layer lstm, 51 inputs, 64 hidden;
  note right
    the dataset was published for unsupervised anomaly
    detection, the labelled split is used here as
    supervised data so the output is a binary verdict
    rather than a continuous score
  end note
  :score the held-out fold;
  :record precision, recall, f1 and auc;
  :benchmark latency on the gpu;
  |me|
  :read the metrics table;
backward :change the class weights and train again;
repeat while (metrics acceptable?) is (no) not (yes)

:select the fold to deploy;
note right
  fold 1 deployed, f1 0.693 at recall 0.929 and
  precision 0.553, five-fold mean f1 0.569 ± 0.077
  auc 0.455 ranks below chance, so the output is a
  binary flag and not a ranking, and a person decides
  every alert
end note
:write the checkpoint into the models directory;
:commit the checkpoint and its sidecar;
:restart ai;

|ai|
:read the architecture, the window length and the
preprocessing constants out of the checkpoint;
note right
  the predictor module is imported from the mounted
  directory at startup, there is no packaged artifact
  and no model-serving process, so a checkpoint reaches
  inference only through a restart
end note
:track a person and extract keypoints;

|redis|
:append the box and keypoints to the track window,
capped at the length the checkpoint declares;

|ai|
if (window full?) then (no)
  :emit warming-up;
  stop
else (yes)
  :run the classifier over two classes;
  if (score at or above threshold?) then (no)
    :emit normal;
    stop
  else (yes)
    :emit anomaly;
    :post the alert with the score and the state;
    :keep the scored window beside the alert;
    note right
      a training example is a full window while the alert
      holds one frame, and the rolling store drops the
      rest within seconds, so the window is kept when the
      alert is raised rather than when it is decided
    end note
  endif
endif

|backend|
:store the alert and its window;

|operator|
:decide confirmed, dismissed or unsure;

|backend|
:store the decision and the actor;
note right
  every decided alert pairs a stored prediction with a
  human label, so live precision and recall are
  countable today
end note
if (decision usable as a label?) then (no)
  :leave the window out of any training set;
  stop
else (yes)
  :add the window to the store dataset;
endif
stop

@enduml
